$\mathrm{A}(0, 0)$, $\mathrm{B}(1, 0)$, $\mathrm{C}(1, 1)$, $\mathrm{D}(0, 1)$이라 하고 $\mathrm{P}(a, b)$라 하면
$\vec{\mathrm{PA}}+\vec{\mathrm{PB}}=2(\vec{\mathrm{PC}}+\vec{\mathrm{PD}})$에서
$(-a, -b)+(1-a, -b)=2((1-a, 1-b)+(-a, 1-b))$;
$(1-2a, -2b)=(2-4a, 4-4b)$; $1-2a=2-4a$, $-2b=4-4b$;
$a=\frac{1}{2}$, $b=2$
$\therefore |\vec{\mathrm{PD}}| = \left|\left(-\frac{1}{2}, -1\right)\right| = \sqrt{\left(-\frac{1}{2}\right)^2+(-1)^2} = \frac{\sqrt{5}}{2}$
